# Line endings.
#
# The team works on Windows and WSL, and a `.env` or `.sh` file that arrives
# with CRLF breaks in ways that look like configuration errors: a `\r` at the end
# of a URL makes Zod report "must be a full URL". Normalise on commit, and keep
# Windows-only artefacts (if any are ever added) as CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Env files are read by dotenv, which tolerates CRLF but not every tool does.
# Configuration templates are the ones that get copied and edited most.
.env* text eol=lf

# Never normalise these: they are binary, or their bytes are the deliverable.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.wasm binary
package-lock.json -diff
